Unchanged 30-child workload, twenty-second wait:
  GCC dying=8, memory.current=438272; EvoCC dying=9, current=344064.
After sequential CPU 0/1/2/3 offline/online, observing one second per CPU:
  GCC dying=6/3/3/0; EvoCC dying=9/6/4/0.
Both stay at zero for another five seconds and shut down normally.
This demonstrates retained per-CPU state on BOTH frozen kernels. Hotplug also
drains object stocks, so it alone does not name one specific reference holder.
Frozen consume_stock nevertheless has the exact empty-slot reference defect
fixed upstream by 48863da10ba1ffe3889fc5945d3292b4e4bf1c60:
https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/08/18/1232
The frozen is_memcg_drain_needed skips zero-page slots. This source evidence
and the causal intervention support the upstream-stock diagnosis, not a
compiler-specific failure. Original test_kmem_dead_cgroups remains FAIL.

Earlier CPU1-pinned variant did not reproduce retained descendants, then
failed on CPU restoration in the HVF lane; not counted as a passing probe.
